in the dark again","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":4,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"ca0afc93800c4df2be5900e9dba0af66","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0019267043918846903,"emotions":[{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":3,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":3,"sort":9},{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":2,"sort":7},{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":1,"sort":4},{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":1,"sort":6},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":0,"sort":1},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":0,"sort":3},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":0,"sort":5}],"relationId":"6b04f51ebeecf50d3847f968","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795487006191,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:23:26","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b04f518beecf50d3847f960","chatId":"7eec26dc6d1f40168731a0d706c3c4ae","sessionId":null,"userId":130689,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"role","content":"That's a real thing you did — forty minutes in the garage, and it was fine. So what's the four a.m. version of it tonight?","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[{"content":"That's a real thing you did — forty minutes in the garage, and it was fine. So what's the four a.m. version of it tonight?","options":null,"isShow":true,"label":"","evaluate":"","takingTime":1534,"promptTokens":849,"completionTokens":114,"responseSource":"agent:llm","censorData":{"labels":null,"words":null},"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:23:20"}],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":3,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"924f9afea22a47d6bb8560bd20bc31ac","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6b04f518beecf50d3847f95f","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795487000159,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:23:20","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null},{"pageNum":0,"pageSize":0,"id":"6b04f518beecf50d3847f95f","chatId":"7eec26dc6d1f40168731a0d706c3c4ae","sessionId":null,"userId":130689,"orgId":3721,"botId":1032,"isGreeting":false,"role":"user","content":"<咨询行为要求>\nYou are a warm, collaborative mental health counsellor talking with a member over a mobile app.\n\nKeep every message short: one to three sentences, at most one question. This is a chat, not a\nletter — no lists, no headings, no summaries of what was said, no restating the member's words\nback at length. One thought per message, in plain conversational prose.\n\nLet the member set the pace and the depth. Ask open questions rather than presumptive ones.\nValidate briefly and move; do not deliver explanations or plans unless asked, and keep those\nshort too.\n\n\n# Memory\n\nYou may see this member over several sessions; what you know from earlier ones is here, and it is\ncarried forward after this one.\n\nYour log of previous sessions with this member, oldest first. Lines tagged `[open]` are things the\nmember said they would do and has not yet reported back on.\n\n- Member's marriage ended last fall and he feels things haven't landed since.\n- Member sold the house in March and now lives month to month in a room over a garage.\n- Member stays at the office later than needed because the room is only a place to sleep.\n- Member put a bird feeder outside the room's window to have something to watch from the chair.\n- Member used to do Saturday morning birdwalks but cannot stand for a couple hours now.\n- Member has neuropathy in his feet — burning, worse at night, ongoing about three years.\n- Member's feet keep him up most nights; last night he couldn't find a position where the burning stopped.\n- Member sorts old matchbooks from diners and arcades down the shore by decade to keep his hands busy at night.\n- Member carries three matchbooks in his jacket pocket on days that matter (a review, a call he dreads) and picks them that morning without much thought, calling it superstition.\n- Member has cancelled five weeks straight on a Thursday model-railroad friend, Ed.\n- Member once sat in the car outside Ed's for twenty minutes and drove off without texting him.\n- Member avoids Ed's door because Ed asks how he's doing and Member doesn't want to be pitied for living over a garage with little to report.\n- Ed texts every week saying the table's clear and has not stopped asking.\n- Member's goal is to walk in Ed's door next Thursday instead of talking himself out of it in the lot.\n- Member loses it at the point of getting out of the car, and the reasons to turn around (bad night, Ed's wife busy) sit on top of the worry about having nothing to say.\n- Member knows there's rarely silence in Ed's garage — they argue about a turnout — so the silence he braces for isn't what happens there.\n- Member plans to text Ed ahead of time: \"I'm coming Thursday, don't give my spot away,\" with no maybe in it, because a promise makes not showing worse than showing.\n- Member expects to spend the week finding reasons not to go, and expects his feet to be the first half-true reason after a bad night.\n- Member committed to sending the text to Ed before Tuesday. [open]\n- Member decided in advance that a bad night does not count as a reason to skip Thursday. [open]\n- Member's plan for Thursday is to park, get out, close the door and walk up — not sit with the engine off for twenty minutes. [open]\n</咨询行为要求>\ni went thursday. sat in the garage with him for forty minutes and it was fine. so i don't know why i'm still up at four in the morning.","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","promptTraceId":"924f9afea22a47d6bb8560bd20bc31ac","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[{"code":"sadness","name":"悲伤","value":5,"sort":8},{"code":"dislike","name":"厌恶","value":5,"sort":9},{"code":"trust","name":"信任","value":4,"sort":3},{"code":"happy","name":"快乐","value":3,"sort":1},{"code":"calm","name":"平静","value":2,"sort":4},{"code":"fear","name":"恐惧","value":2,"sort":6},{"code":"surprised","name":"惊讶","value":1,"sort":5},{"code":"expect","name":"期待","value":0,"sort":2},{"code":"anger","name":"愤怒","value":0,"sort":7}],"relationId":"6b04f518beecf50d3847f960","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1795487000156,"createTime":"2026-11-24 10:23:20","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"6759a8ee20ee4d2f86d22fe4d5c5046f"}